con-sŏcer ,
		ĕri, m.; -crus , ūs, f.;
		a designation of the fathers and mothers of a married pair, 
I.a joint
			father-in-law or mother-in-law; one of two
				fathers-in-law or mothers-in-law;
			masc., Suet. Claud. 29; Dig. 24, 1, 32, § 20 sq.;
					Aus. Parent. Mart. 10, 33,
			3.—* Fem.,
					Aus. Parent. 30 inscr.
